[2026-09-21 15:12:32 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 108] verdict: On the full CometEls near-parabolic census (n=268), the aphelia lean toward the cap-declaration axis at d_par=+0.104 under the identical tide-aware null (p=0.0007); the spike-proxy subset (n=115) leans at +0.178 (p=0.0005).  The 206 comets absent from the 229-comet training set -- the genuinely new information -- lean at +0.071 (p=0.0309).  The census's own free dipole recovers (35,-34), 21 deg from the cap axis and 159 deg from the anti-axis -- the broadest discovered population self-organizes toward the measured sector without being told where it is.
